-- title:
--   Corner realisation at minimal level and its base identification
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$; let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a $2$-dimensional $k$-space with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ trivial on the absolute group of some number field) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$. Let $S,S_{\min}$ be finite sets of naturals with every member of $S$ prime, $p\in S_{\min}\subseteq S$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (some inertia element at some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $q$ acts non-trivially), and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N\neq 0$ be squarefree, with every prime factor in $S$, with every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$ dividing $N$, and with every prime factor $q\neq p$ of $N$ in $S_{\min}$; let $r$ be a natural number, and assume weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by forms with integral $q$-expansions. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. The assertion is that there exist a type $M$ with an abelian group structure, a module structure over the localisation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and over $\mathcal{O}$, compatible as a scalar tower, with $M$ finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, and an $\mathcal{O}$-bilinear form $B:M\times M\to\mathcal{O}$, such that two things hold. First, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.IsCornerRealization p ρbar N N S θ M B`](def/CuspForm_HeckeModuleCornerRealization.html#L19): there are a commuting family of the Hecke and diamond operators `opFamily` indexed by [`CohCarrier.Gen N S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) acting on $H^1=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal{O})$, a character $\bar\theta$ on these generators, an idempotent splitting $\mathrm{Sp}$ of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra they generate, an index $i_0$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring at $i_0$ to $k$, and an $\mathcal{O}$-linear isomorphism of $M$ with the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1$, whose elements are all parabolic homomorphisms; here $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\bar\theta(U_q)=0$ whenever $q^2\mid N$, $\bar\theta(U_p)\neq 0$ if $p\mid N$ and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, $\pi_k$ sends the image of each generator in the corner ring to its $\bar\theta$-value, the isomorphism intertwines the action of the image $\pi(T_\ell)$ in `heckeLocal` with `heckeT` at $\ell$, and $B$ is the pairing [`CuspForm.Bfam₀ 𝒪 N`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140) transported along it. Secondly, if $p\mid N$ implies that $\bar\rho$ is not finite flat at $p$ in the sense of [`GaloisRepAdic.IsFlatAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L29), then the operators `baseOp` indexed by the generators $g\in$ [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.Gen N r S`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L11) (primes $\ell_g\notin S$ with $\ell_g\nmid N$ and $\ell_g\neq r$) commute on $H^1$, and for such a commutation witness $hc_0$ there is an $\mathcal{O}$-linear isomorphism of $M$ with [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.baseML N r S 𝒪 θ hc₀`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModuleBase.html#L31) carrying, for each generator $g$ and each $m\in M$, the action of $\pi(T_{\ell_g})$ on $m$ to the action of the polynomial variable `MvPolynomial.X g` of the free algebra $\mathcal{O}[X_g]$ on the image of $m$.
--
--   This is the bottom rung of the tower of Hecke modules used in the Taylor–Wiles argument: at the minimal level $N$ attached to $\bar\rho$ it produces a finite free $\mathcal{O}$-module with an action of the localised anemic Hecke algebra, realised as an idempotent corner of the parabolic cohomology $\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal{O})$ equipped with the Poincaré-type pairing, and identifies that corner with the free-algebra module `baseML` except in the finite flat case at $p\mid N$. It is cited in the construction of the level-raising chain of Hecke modules.
